# TAHINI SAUCE WITH GARLIC AND LEMON
## info
* About 10 minutes prep, 10 minutes total
* Makes about 2 cups

## ingredients
* 2/3 cup fresh lemon juice (from 3 to 4 lemons)
* 1 whole head garlic, broken into individual unpeeled cloves (about 20 cloves)
* 1 generous cup tahini paste (about 10 oz)
* 1/2 teaspoon ground cumin
* cold water, as needed
* kosher salt, to taste

## steps
1. Combine the lemon juice and garlic cloves in a blender. Blend until the garlic is completely pulverized into a rough pulp.
1. Pour the mixture through a fine-mesh strainer into a large bowl, pressing firmly to extract as much lemon-garlic liquid as possible. Discard the solids.
1. Add the tahini paste and cumin to the bowl. Whisk until combined.
1. Gradually whisk in cold water a little at a time. The mixture will initially thicken, then loosen into a smooth, pale, creamy sauce.
1. Season with kosher salt to taste.
1. Continue adding cold water until the sauce reaches your desired consistency.
1. Serve immediately or refrigerate in a sealed container until needed.

